note tools/gen/retrieval/genret.om -- file-backed retrieval provider of the GEN experiment (aien-spark/omega#479,
note #475), pure OM-2. Contract: tools/gen/retrieval/CONTRACT.md (genret-cli-v3). Arms C and D run the same
note algorithm with the same k, byte cap and rendering; only --kind differs. The query is built from the public
note requirement (entry, params, ret values) and the public prompt only; no other task file is opened.
note
note   genret query --corpus <MANIFEST> --manifest-sha256 <hex> --recheck <recheck binary> --recheck-sha256 <hex>
note                --kind raw|abstraction --k <n> --cap-bytes <n>
note                --requirement <file> --prompt <file> --out <new dir> [--exclude-family <f>]...
note                [--mode normal|irrelevant|empty|length-matched] [--target-bytes <n>]
note   genret version
note
note Exit 0 on success (an empty selection included); exit 2 on any fatal condition, with one stderr line
note "genret: FATAL <reason> <detail>" and no --out. All scoring is integer arithmetic (BM25 numerator and
note denominator in 128 bits, as two ulong words).
note
note Built by mk/gen-retrieval.mk as one unit: seed/ng/sha256.om (sh_*), a generated binding unit that
note defines `text gr_bin_pin` (the sha256 of the recheck binary built in the same make run, or "" for the
note test-only genret_anyrecheck) and `text gr_src_claim` (the verified recheck source sha256, or
note "unverified"), then this file.
note
note Validator execution: genret hashes the --recheck file through one open descriptor and executes that same
note open file. execprog closes every descriptor at or above 3, so the child first duplicates the hashed
note descriptor onto descriptor 0 and executes /proc/self/fd/0 (the open file, not the path, as fexecve
note does); recheck reads no standard input. The child's environment is empty (execprog), and its argument
note zero is /proc/self/fd/0. A batch holds at most 128 records and at most 65536 packet bytes (the execprog
note limit); batch size does not change what is accepted, since every record must get its own OK line.
note Paths: a path over 4095 bytes is treated as one that cannot be opened (the C got ENAMETOOLONG). The final
note rename passes both paths in one renames list of at most 4096 bytes; a longer pair is write_failed.

